   "going_concern_summary": "Invacare's 2022 statements were still prepared on a going-concern basis, but management's required evaluation flagged conditions bearing on substantial doubt, because on 31 January 2023 the company and two U.S. subsidiaries filed voluntary chapter 11 petitions in the U.S. Bankruptcy Court for the Southern District of Texas. Whether the company can carry on as a going concern therefore depends on the court approving and the company implementing a plan of reorganization, emerging from chapter 11, and producing enough liquidity afterwards to meet its obligations and operating needs; the bankruptcy process itself adds significant risk and uncertainty."
