 "checks": "Reference values all confirmed: net sales 872,457 (2021) / 850,689 (2020) / 927,964 (2019) / 741,733 (2022); operating cash flow (14,309) 2021 and (55,251) 2022; total equity 218,489 (2021), 81,092 (2022), 308,516 (2019). Income statements: gross profit = revenues - cost of products sold, and net loss = loss before income taxes - tax provision, exact for every year 2019-2022. Operating income and loss before taxes also tie exactly, provided the expense-style layout is read as printed (positive amounts are deducted; a negative amount, e.g. gain on sale of business (9,790) or debt extinguishment (9,422), is a credit). OCI components sum to OCI and net loss + OCI = comprehensive income in every year. Balance sheets (2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022): current assets, total assets, current liabilities, equity components and total liabilities and equity all reconcile exactly. Cash flows (FY2021 10-K, 2021/2020/2019): operating, investing and financing subtotals reconcile exactly; CFO+CFI+CFF+FX = net change, and opening cash + change = closing cash, for all three years. FY2022 10-K: investing, financing, net change and the cash roll-forward reconcile exactly for 2022 and 2021, and the 2021 operating section reconciles exactly. The 2022 operating lines available sum to (65,626) against the printed (55,251), a gap of 10,375 (see gaps). Debt tables: instruments sum to the totals (308,129 / 245,053 in the 2021 10-K; 354,241 / 308,129 in the 2022 10-K). Total less current maturities = long-term debt, which matches the balance sheet (305,022 / 239,441 / 354,087).",
 "gaps": "All values come from SEC XBRL R pages read through WebFetch, a summarising model, not from the printed 10-K pages. Row labels are the R-page labels: XBRL standard labels such as 'Revenues' (printed as Net sales) and 'Gain (Loss) on Extinguishment of Debt' may differ from the printed wording. EPS is in US$ and share counts in thousands. Reordering and omissions: on the R pages the common-share and Class B rows sit at the bottom of the balance sheet. They were moved into the equity section, where the printed 10-K shows them. XBRL-only rows were dropped: preferred shares authorised/outstanding counts, and the duplicate items rendered above the cash-flow table ('Purchases of capped calls' and others). Sign corrections (flagged): the R pages show the cash-flow line 'Loss (gain) on debt extinguishment...' with the opposite sign to what the statements need: +9,422 / -7,360 / -6,165 in the 2021 10-K and +9,419 / +9,422 / -7,360 in the 2022 10-K. Flipping only this line makes the operating subtotals reconcile exactly for 2019, 2020 and 2021 in both filings, and it agrees with the income statement. So the stored values are -9,422 (2021), +7,360 (2020), +6,165 (2019) and -9,419 (2022). In the 2022 10-K R5, the 2021 'Provision for other deferred liabilities' shows (160) while the 2021 10-K shows 160. 160 is stored because only it reconciles. Filled from the other filing (flagged): the 2022 10-K R3 omits the 2021 value of 'Long-Term Obligations - Finance Leases'. 63,736 is taken from the 2021 10-K, and the 2021 column then reconciles exactly. The 2022 10-K R5 leaves 2021 'Cash and cash equivalents at beginning of year' blank, so 105,298 comes from the 2021 10-K. Unresolved, 2022 operating cash flow: the XBRL calculation linkbase shows that the printed operating section also includes Inventory write-down, Other noncash income and Other noncash expense lines. R5 shows Inventory write-down blank for 2022 and Other Noncash Income 573 (placement and sign as printed are unknown), so the 2022 operating lines leave a 10,375 gap. The Inventories details page (R73) tags an Inventory write-down of 8,651 (context labelled Sep. 30, 2022). An exact tie would follow if the write-down is 8,651 and the 2022 provision for receivables is +862 rather than (862), but that is unconfirmed, so 2022 Inventory write-down is left null. Treat the 2022 values of provision for losses, provision for other deferred liabilities and Other Noncash Income as sign-uncertain. Other: the 2022 10-K statements also contain a 2020 column, which was not captured, per scope. The 2019 10-K balance sheet (R4) common-share labels carry no authorised/issued detail in what was retrieved. The going-concern text on R36 was truncated after the start of the risk list; the summary rests on the retrieved paragraphs. The printed 10-K document (ivc-20221231.htm) was too large for WebFetch to reach Item 8, and the data.sec.gov API and direct curl were unavailable."
